1
00:00:19,810 --> 00:00:23,590
If doing that means no one will cry, then...

2
00:01:56,180 --> 00:02:00,520
{\an4}Idealism's End

3
00:01:56,180 --> 00:02:00,520
{\an4}THE ANSWER

4
00:02:20,570 --> 00:02:24,420
You certainly took your time getting here, Emiya Shirou.

5
00:02:25,050 --> 00:02:27,870
It finally occurred to me.

6
00:02:27,870 --> 00:02:30,320
There can't be two of those pendants.

7
00:02:31,060 --> 00:02:31,940
It was originally—

8
00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:32,600
That's right.

9
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:40,350
After your life was saved, you carried it for the rest of your days.

10
00:02:40,970 --> 00:02:44,570
A memento of Tohsaka Rin's father, unique in all the world.

11
00:02:45,110 --> 00:02:48,520
When summoning a Heroic Spirit, a catalyst is needed.

12
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:52,320
But Tohsaka Rin did not have one for the invocation.

13
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:53,630
Because of that,

14
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:57,580
she assumed that she had no connection to the Servant she summoned.

15
00:02:58,460 --> 00:03:02,190
But no Heroic Spirit is summoned by chance.

16
00:03:02,190 --> 00:03:06,040
A link is always required between summoner and spirit.

17
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:09,260
If Rin had no catalyst, that means...

18
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,660
Yes.

19
00:03:10,660 --> 00:03:16,390
The summoned Heroic Spirit,
not the summoner, possessed the catalyst.

20
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:19,990
The concept of time does not exist
where the Heroic Spirits are recorded.

21
00:03:20,730 --> 00:03:24,270
Heroic Spirits from the past are treated identically to those of the future.

22
00:03:25,050 --> 00:03:26,020
In short...

23
00:03:26,590 --> 00:03:27,370
Yes.

24
00:03:27,910 --> 00:03:33,830
It is possible to summon someone who will exist in the future.

25
00:03:33,830 --> 00:03:34,780
Archer...

26
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:37,020
Where's Tohsaka?

27
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:39,790
I handed her over to Matou Shinji when he got here before you.

28
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:41,040
You what?

29
00:03:41,040 --> 00:03:42,830
Relax, kid.

30
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:46,190
Leave the little lady to me.

31
00:03:46,190 --> 00:03:47,660
Lancer?

32
00:03:47,660 --> 00:03:50,190
I have my Master's orders, you see.

33
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:54,720
Keeping her alive has always been my reason for working with you.

34
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:58,190
Actually, it's been really nice.

35
00:03:58,190 --> 00:04:02,100
It's rare for me to enjoy a task I've been given.

36
00:04:02,590 --> 00:04:05,480
So until this is over, let me look after her.

37
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:08,980
After that, we'll be enemies again.

38
00:04:13,550 --> 00:04:15,160
Take care of Tohsaka.

39
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:16,240
Will do.

40
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:23,720
I shall remain here, Lancer.

41
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:25,090
Are you serious?

42
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:27,120
The little lady is your Master now.

43
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,330
I understand that.

44
00:04:29,330 --> 00:04:33,560
But I must bear witness to this battle.

45
00:04:36,170 --> 00:04:37,500
Really now?

46
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:38,780
Have it your way, then.

47
00:04:41,290 --> 00:04:43,390
"Bear witness," huh?

48
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:45,400
I'm glad to hear that.

49
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:51,720
If you interfered now, severing my contract
with Rin would have been for nothing.

50
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:53,090
Yes.

51
00:04:53,090 --> 00:04:56,660
Come what may, I will not interfere with your battle with Shirou.

52
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:59,980
But in return, I want you to answer one thing.

53
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:02,660
Why are you so intent on killing Shirou?

54
00:05:03,080 --> 00:05:05,450
Why do you even ask?

55
00:05:05,450 --> 00:05:10,990
Just as he can't accept me, I can't accept him. That's all.

56
00:05:10,990 --> 00:05:12,700
That cannot be true!

57
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:17,430
You should embody Emiya Shirou's ideals in the form of a hero.

58
00:05:17,730 --> 00:05:20,930
Why would that ideal reject itself?

59
00:05:21,430 --> 00:05:26,760
Unlike you, I didn't become a hero entirely on my own merits.

60
00:05:26,760 --> 00:05:31,940
I'm nothing but a Guardian who became a hero
by selling his posthumous self.

61
00:05:32,340 --> 00:05:33,340
A Guardian?

62
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:37,260
Off you go.

63
00:05:45,870 --> 00:05:47,920
What's with the glare?

64
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:51,760
I see you're as oblivious as ever.

65
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,710
Don't you understand the position you're in?

66
00:05:55,090 --> 00:05:57,110
Try looking in a mirror.

67
00:05:57,110 --> 00:05:59,810
I'd say you're the oblivious one here.

68
00:05:59,810 --> 00:06:01,770
Oh, drop the tough act.

69
00:06:01,770 --> 00:06:03,100
It's pathetic.

70
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:06,790
Unbelievable.

71
00:06:06,790 --> 00:06:08,850
Looks like nothing I say will get through to you.

72
00:06:08,850 --> 00:06:12,070
Good! That's more like it!

73
00:06:12,070 --> 00:06:16,150
So you've finally figured out that you belong to me?

74
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:21,660
Man, I love legs that have just enough muscle.

75
00:06:22,740 --> 00:06:25,910
It'll make playing with you all the more fun.

76
00:06:26,230 --> 00:06:26,870
Ow!

77
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:37,740
Sorry about that, punk.

78
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:40,090
My fist went flying before my words.

79
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:43,220
L-Lancer?

80
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,100
Hey.

81
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:47,750
Wh-What are you doing here?

82
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:48,890
Save it.

83
00:06:48,890 --> 00:06:51,060
I'll have those ropes cut in a jiffy.

84
00:06:51,060 --> 00:06:52,360
After that, do as you like.

85
00:06:52,740 --> 00:06:55,780
Go to the hall and stop those idiots from fighting,

86
00:06:55,780 --> 00:06:57,740
or slip out the back and go home. Your call.

87
00:06:58,490 --> 00:06:59,610
Lancer, behind you!

88
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:01,620
What?

89
00:07:02,310 --> 00:07:04,370
That's quite enough, Lancer.

90
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:08,120
I did say to work with them,

91
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:13,280
but I never said to get emotionally invested.

92
00:07:14,130 --> 00:07:15,600
Kirei?

93
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,550
A Guardian?

94
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:23,410
I heard that, after their deaths, Guardians become part of the Counter Force that protects humanity.

95
00:07:23,410 --> 00:07:27,180
Even if you followed a different path to become one,
you are nonetheless a Heroic Spirit.

96
00:07:27,490 --> 00:07:29,900
That's where you're mistaken, Saber.

97
00:07:29,900 --> 00:07:32,690
Guardians don't protect humanity.

98
00:07:32,690 --> 00:07:34,810
They're simply sweepers.

99
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:36,320
Archer?

100
00:07:36,580 --> 00:07:37,670
You're right...

101
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:40,620
I did become a hero.

102
00:07:40,620 --> 00:07:44,110
Just as the man called Emiya Shirou always wished,

103
00:07:44,110 --> 00:07:46,700
I became a true champion of justice.

104
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:52,030
A champion of justice...

105
00:07:52,650 --> 00:07:55,210
And that is exactly why.

106
00:07:55,210 --> 00:07:58,490
I know that becoming one was a mistake.

107
00:07:58,490 --> 00:08:02,720
That man's life had absolutely no value.

108
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,790
No value?

109
00:08:04,790 --> 00:08:05,590
None.

110
00:08:06,150 --> 00:08:08,090
Surely you understand, Saber.

111
00:08:08,090 --> 00:08:13,480
After all, you want to change the past—
to take back your decisions—more than anyone.

112
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,000
Saber?

113
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:16,610
What?

114
00:08:16,610 --> 00:08:18,470
You never asked her what her wish was?

115
00:08:18,470 --> 00:08:25,620
Why she desires the Holy Grail enough
to commit herself to this pointless bloodbath?

116
00:08:27,690 --> 00:08:30,640
Then allow me to tell you. She is—

117
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:31,620
Archer!

118
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,040
Shirou...

119
00:08:40,790 --> 00:08:44,940
I wanted to use the Holy Grail—the all-powerful granter of wishes—

120
00:08:45,910 --> 00:08:48,260
to undo a decision I once made.

121
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,530
I made a mistake—

122
00:09:10,600 --> 00:09:13,160
one that condemned Britain to destruction.

123
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,120
And I fell before I could change that fate.

124
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:21,020
That is why I want to win the Grail.

125
00:09:24,090 --> 00:09:26,130
I did not reach my ideal self.

126
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:29,850
I should never have become king.

127
00:09:29,850 --> 00:09:31,340
But you are different.

128
00:09:31,950 --> 00:09:36,020
Are you not the ideals of Emiya Shirou fully realized?

129
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:39,270
The realized ideals, huh?

130
00:09:41,410 --> 00:09:46,400
It's true that I did become my own ideal champion of justice.

131
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:50,440
But as a result, I gained nothing but regrets.

132
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:54,160
Having made a pact with the Counter Force when alive,

133
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:56,790
I became a Guardian after my death

134
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,650
and acted on behalf of humanity's Counter Force,

135
00:09:59,650 --> 00:10:02,550
fighting those who disrupted the world's balance.

136
00:10:03,190 --> 00:10:05,340
Obeying my orders,

137
00:10:06,040 --> 00:10:07,260
I killed.

138
00:10:07,590 --> 00:10:08,510
And killed...

139
00:10:09,540 --> 00:10:10,930
And just kept killing.

140
00:10:13,450 --> 00:10:16,350
I killed so many I ceased to care.

141
00:10:16,950 --> 00:10:20,860
For every life I took, I saved thousands.

142
00:10:23,350 --> 00:10:26,600
I fought again and again, whenever I was called upon.

143
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:33,280
Again,

144
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:36,160
and again,

145
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:37,960
and again...

146
00:10:39,230 --> 00:10:43,000
But there was no end to it.

147
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,870
It was never over.

148
00:10:44,870 --> 00:10:49,760
It wasn't as if I dreamed of a world free of fighting.

149
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:57,690
I just didn't want anyone to cry in the world I knew.

150
00:10:58,730 --> 00:11:01,180
That's when it finally hit me.

151
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:06,530
The ideal that Emiya Shirou clung to was but shallow idealism.

152
00:11:07,130 --> 00:11:08,560
Why do you say that?

153
00:11:09,610 --> 00:11:12,540
It's impossible to save everyone.

154
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:19,200
Saving the many means leaving the few to perish.

155
00:11:19,200 --> 00:11:22,180
You should know that well, Saber.

156
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:27,160
Those who were bound to fall from the seat of happiness,

157
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,370
I quickly cut down with my own hands.

158
00:11:30,150 --> 00:11:35,850
That is the proper course of action for a hero—
for that man's ideal champion of justice.

159
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:40,720
Saving as many as possible is what a champion of justice does, is it not?

160
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:44,300
And so, still wishing for no one to die,

161
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:47,360
I would have one person die for the sake of many.

162
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:50,250
Even as I said that I couldn't let anyone feel sorrow,

163
00:11:50,740 --> 00:11:55,240
I ultimately drove more than a few to despair.

164
00:11:59,510 --> 00:12:01,500
That is who I am.

165
00:12:01,500 --> 00:12:04,560
That is the Heroic Spirit Emiya's true colors.

166
00:12:04,560 --> 00:12:09,340
Don't you think the world would be better off
if that man died right now?

167
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:25,120
Kill yourself, Emiya Shirou.

168
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:28,710
Ow...

169
00:12:28,710 --> 00:12:33,610
Wasn't it my Master's credo to never reveal themselves?

170
00:12:33,610 --> 00:12:35,990
I have no such policy.

171
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:40,640
In fact, you are the one disobeying orders, Lancer.

172
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:43,720
I seem to recall ordering you to terminate Archer.

173
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:47,140
He'll do himself in without any help from me.

174
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:50,590
More importantly, did you put that kid up to this?

175
00:12:51,050 --> 00:12:53,350
Spare me your baseless accusations.

176
00:12:53,350 --> 00:12:55,920
We have an arrangement.

177
00:12:55,920 --> 00:13:00,430
We've reached a mutual accord for the sake of winning the Grail.

178
00:13:00,430 --> 00:13:01,870
Figures.

179
00:13:01,870 --> 00:13:05,240
I always knew you wouldn't die that easily,

180
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:09,020
but why win a harmless loser like Shinji over to your side?

181
00:13:09,020 --> 00:13:12,330
You take him for harmless, do you?

182
00:13:12,330 --> 00:13:16,910
Even in this situation, you remain Tohsaka Rin to the core.

183
00:13:17,350 --> 00:13:22,200
If you were a less capable pupil, this would be less regrettable.

184
00:13:22,570 --> 00:13:24,470
Hang on, Kotomine.

185
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:29,460
Was that talk about wanting to save your pupil a lie?

186
00:13:30,990 --> 00:13:32,580
Nothing of the sort.

187
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:36,440
She is an important pawn that I have taken great pains to nurture.

188
00:13:36,440 --> 00:13:39,530
I've spent ten long years deceiving her,

189
00:13:39,530 --> 00:13:42,470
so what fun would it be if she left the battle so easily?

190
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:46,630
That was why I entrusted her safety to you.

191
00:13:47,850 --> 00:13:49,300
You phony priest.

192
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:53,940
Participating in a game that you're supposed to oversee is so unfair it's not even funny.

193
00:13:53,940 --> 00:13:57,900
And yet you don't seem all that surprised, Rin.

194
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:00,410
So you suspected me?

195
00:14:00,410 --> 00:14:02,290
Of course I did.

196
00:14:02,290 --> 00:14:06,370
Though admittedly, it never occurred to me that I'd been tricked from the beginning.

197
00:14:06,690 --> 00:14:08,780
From the beginning?

198
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:09,670
What?

199
00:14:10,280 --> 00:14:13,070
Oh, when you said, "From the beginning,"

200
00:14:13,070 --> 00:14:16,040
I was wondering how far back you meant.

201
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:19,260
Kirei, you...

202
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:23,660
Since after this Holy Grail War began?

203
00:14:23,660 --> 00:14:26,310
Or does the "beginning" you speak of

204
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:30,170
refer to the previous Holy Grail War?

205
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,920
I see...

206
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:41,240
So it was you who killed my father.

207
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:42,980
Of course.

208
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:44,990
After all, he was my beloved teacher.

209
00:14:45,590 --> 00:14:48,370
Catching him by surprise was child's play.

210
00:14:51,360 --> 00:14:52,630
What's the matter?

211
00:14:52,630 --> 00:14:55,140
Now that you know what you are, why hesitate?

212
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:56,460
Archer,

213
00:14:56,810 --> 00:14:59,290
you have not gone against your ideals.

214
00:14:59,290 --> 00:15:01,410
Did you not simply lose your way

215
00:15:01,410 --> 00:15:03,720
when the very ideals you upheld betrayed you?

216
00:15:04,110 --> 00:15:05,650
Were that not the case,

217
00:15:05,650 --> 00:15:09,050
you would not consider killing yourself atonement for your sins.

218
00:15:14,900 --> 00:15:17,210
Oh, this is rich.

219
00:15:17,210 --> 00:15:19,860
Atone for my sins?

220
00:15:20,190 --> 00:15:22,250
Don't be a fool, Saber.

221
00:15:23,150 --> 00:15:27,140
You're right: I was betrayed and deceived countless times.

222
00:15:27,770 --> 00:15:33,250
You can't expect anyone to understand a man willing to lay down his life for others.

223
00:15:33,870 --> 00:15:35,080
In the end,

224
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:38,970
I was set up as the mastermind behind a conflict and sent to the gallows.

225
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:41,130
You must be lying, Archer...

226
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:43,570
That was how you died?

227
00:15:45,430 --> 00:15:50,230
If I had any sins, surely I atoned fully for them in that moment.

228
00:15:50,640 --> 00:15:54,500
It's not as if I ever wanted gratitude.

229
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:57,650
I never wanted to be celebrated as a hero, either.

230
00:15:57,650 --> 00:16:01,940
I simply wanted an outcome where everyone was happy.

231
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:04,270
But that was never given to me—

232
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:06,490
neither in life nor afterward.

233
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:11,380
I knew that Guardians were, essentially, automated defense mechanisms.

234
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:14,580
That after death, those who offer themselves to be Guardians

235
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:16,740
are removed from the cycle of death and rebirth,

236
00:16:16,740 --> 00:16:19,470
becoming tools that safeguard human history.

237
00:16:20,250 --> 00:16:24,060
I thought it would still be worth it if I could save someone—

238
00:16:24,060 --> 00:16:26,180
one person who was in trouble.

239
00:16:26,460 --> 00:16:28,170
But it's nothing like that!

240
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:29,180
You bastard!

241
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:31,520
I hope you get lost in the afterlife, you asshole!

242
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:34,310
Even Hell wouldn't want anything to do with you!

243
00:16:34,310 --> 00:16:38,570
Purgatory would call you a bad influence and pass you off somewhere else!

244
00:16:38,570 --> 00:16:40,260
But I'm sure you'd just hate it in Heaven,

245
00:16:40,260 --> 00:16:44,570
so why don't you string yourself up outside the Pearly Gates, you eunuch?!

246
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:52,620
Kotomine, you know that Tohsaka's been given to me, right?

247
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:55,310
I'm the only one who has business with her.

248
00:16:55,310 --> 00:16:57,670
No, I have business with her as well.

249
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:02,510
You see, I require her to become the Holy Grail.

250
00:17:04,110 --> 00:17:08,590
Once Archer and Saber are gone, the time will finally be right.

251
00:17:08,590 --> 00:17:12,620
I do not want her to lose her freshness by resisting needlessly.

252
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:15,600
Let us get this over with quickly.

253
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:19,080
Lancer, dispose of that trash.

254
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:21,610
The vessel has no need of a heart.

255
00:17:21,940 --> 00:17:24,640
Guardians don't save humans.

256
00:17:24,640 --> 00:17:27,280
Guardians simply clean up their messes.

257
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:33,450
They're beings that use their power to negate events that have already transpired—

258
00:17:33,450 --> 00:17:35,690
disasters of humanity's own making.

259
00:17:36,230 --> 00:17:42,410
They're butchers that kill anyone who threatens the human world, with no regard for good and evil.

260
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:45,350
What a joke.

261
00:17:45,350 --> 00:17:48,490
How is that any different from when I was powerless?

262
00:17:48,490 --> 00:17:50,750
To save as many lives as possible...

263
00:17:51,630 --> 00:17:57,270
Are you saying that you were unable to fulfill that wish even once?

264
00:17:57,720 --> 00:17:59,130
I am.

265
00:17:59,130 --> 00:18:04,850
I've culled the very people I wanted to save.

266
00:18:04,850 --> 00:18:08,280
That was where my ridiculous ideal of becoming a champion of justice ultimately lead.

267
00:18:08,980 --> 00:18:11,290
I'm sick of cleaning up after humanity.

268
00:18:11,290 --> 00:18:15,490
But as a Heroic Spirit, I'm doomed to repeat that for all eternity.

269
00:18:16,300 --> 00:18:18,500
I've already given up my agency.

270
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:21,630
The only way I can think of to disappear completely would be...

271
00:18:21,990 --> 00:18:25,150
If you kill a human destined to be a hero,

272
00:18:25,150 --> 00:18:28,800
you think it will be as though that hero was never born?

273
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:34,060
My only hope has been to wait for that opportunity—
for this day to come.

274
00:18:34,680 --> 00:18:36,480
It will not work.

275
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:39,880
You already exist as a Guardian.

276
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,980
You are outside the confines of time.

277
00:18:43,030 --> 00:18:47,570
Even if you eliminate this Shirou, you will not disappear.

278
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:49,310
Perhaps.

279
00:18:49,310 --> 00:18:52,890
But it isn't beyond the realm of possibility.

280
00:18:52,890 --> 00:18:57,250
If I destroy not only his flesh but also his spirit,

281
00:18:57,250 --> 00:19:03,750
at the very least, his mistaken
"champion of justice" will not appear in this world.

282
00:19:04,390 --> 00:19:06,210
What's the matter, Emiya Shirou?

283
00:19:06,210 --> 00:19:08,420
If I'm so unacceptable to you,

284
00:19:08,420 --> 00:19:10,500
kill yourself right here and end it!

285
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:17,760
Shirou!

286
00:19:19,030 --> 00:19:20,730
What's the matter, Lancer?

287
00:19:20,730 --> 00:19:22,940
Your target is a little girl.

288
00:19:22,940 --> 00:19:25,150
Killing her should be simple.

289
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:28,160
I refuse.

290
00:19:28,160 --> 00:19:29,900
I can't obey you this time.

291
00:19:30,460 --> 00:19:31,740
What?

292
00:19:32,330 --> 00:19:34,260
If you want to make me do it,

293
00:19:34,260 --> 00:19:36,580
you'll have to use a Command Spell.

294
00:19:38,890 --> 00:19:41,030
You leave me no choice, then.

295
00:19:45,800 --> 00:19:48,210
In that case, I order you by my Command Spell:

296
00:19:50,010 --> 00:19:51,730
Sorry, Emiya-kun.

297
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:54,290
I'm leaving this fight before you.

298
00:19:55,680 --> 00:19:58,640
Kill yourself, Lancer.

299
00:20:17,370 --> 00:20:18,610
Lancer!

300
00:20:22,030 --> 00:20:25,990
Archer, do you have regrets?

301
00:20:25,990 --> 00:20:27,100
Of course I do.

302
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:34,930
Then I guess we're two different people after all.

303
00:20:34,930 --> 00:20:36,180
What?

304
00:20:38,560 --> 00:20:42,570
No matter what happens, I'll never regret a thing.

305
00:20:42,570 --> 00:20:45,860
And that's why I'll never accept you.

306
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:48,970
If you're my ideal,

307
00:20:48,970 --> 00:20:52,840
then I'll just have to get rid of that misguided ideal myself!

308
00:20:53,540 --> 00:20:56,760
That way of thinking is how all of this began.

309
00:20:56,760 --> 00:21:00,240
One day, you will reach the point where you become me.

310
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,390
I won't.

311
00:21:01,390 --> 00:21:03,580
That day will never come.

312
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:05,120
That's true.

313
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,640
I suppose it won't.

314
00:21:07,370 --> 00:21:11,510
If you won't run from here, in any event, you have no future.

315
00:21:16,780 --> 00:21:17,680
Archer!

316
00:21:17,680 --> 00:21:19,760
It's okay, Saber.

317
00:21:19,760 --> 00:21:20,750
Thanks.

318
00:21:21,510 --> 00:21:23,480
But please, stand back.

319
00:21:26,260 --> 00:21:29,360
This is a fight I need to have.

320
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:31,730
Trace...

321
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:33,900
...on.

322
00:21:39,930 --> 00:21:42,370
Can you keep up with my blade works?

323
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:47,580
If your precision wavers even slightly, it will spell your death.

324
00:22:04,570 --> 00:22:10,190
If I am destined to turn to ash and bones

325
00:23:26,690 --> 00:23:28,790
I will take your heart.

326
00:23:28,790 --> 00:23:31,560
Once useless, always useless, I suppose.

327
00:23:31,560 --> 00:23:35,400
I admired the wish to save someone, because it was beautiful!

328
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:40,060
I don't want to become one. I will become one!

329
00:23:37,610 --> 00:23:41,070
Next Time

